cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "faust-icc: in-car communication with adaptive howling suppression in FAUST"
message: "If you use this code, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chakraborty
    given-names: Ashmita
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A FAUST library for in-car communication (ITU-T P.1150), treating the problem
  as closed-loop feedback control rather than speech enhancement. Provides a
  gain ceiling referenced to measured maximum stable gain, a filterbank howling
  detector that separates feedback modes from speech formants by persistence, a
  self-allocating cascade of adaptive notches, and frequency-shift
  decorrelation. Includes a synthetic cabin model so the whole system is
  demonstrable without hardware.
keywords:
  - in-car communication
  - acoustic feedback
  - howling suppression
  - FAUST
  - audio DSP
